1
00:00:00,882 --> 00:00:08,637
Welcome to Australia's states, part 1 of 1. First, I clear the chosen names
for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:20,515
We work through 8 of the Australia regions the map names, once each: where it
sits, one fact worth keeping, and a hook to remember it by.

3
00:00:21,174 --> 00:00:23,554
Let's bring Northern Territory into view.

4
00:00:28,788 --> 00:00:40,514
The Northern Territory is a territory, not a state, and it fills the middle
north of the continent between Western Australia and Queensland, with Darwin
on the Timor Sea.

5
00:00:41,172 --> 00:00:55,824
The giant red rock Uluru is here, and it was handed back to its Anangu owners
in 1985 and leased back as a national park, while the territory holds a sixth
of the land with only about one per cent of the people.

6
00:00:56,483 --> 00:01:02,880
Remember the red rock in the middle of the country and a northern territory
that never became a state.

7
00:01:03,567 --> 00:01:05,692
Let's bring Queensland into view.

8
00:01:10,928 --> 00:01:19,972
Queensland is the big north-eastern state, reaching from the Northern
Territory border to the Coral Sea, with Brisbane on its south-east coast.

9
00:01:20,627 --> 00:01:39,167
The Great Barrier Reef runs for 2,300 kilometres along this coast, the largest
structure on earth built by living things, and the Daintree rainforest at the
far north is the oldest continuously surviving rainforest in the world.

10
00:01:39,825 --> 00:01:47,580
Remember the coral coast with the great reef running beside it and the oldest
rainforest still growing right down to the shore.

11
00:01:48,261 --> 00:01:51,071
Let's bring Western Australia into view.

12
00:01:54,740 --> 00:02:05,444
Western Australia fills the whole western third of the continent, from the
Northern Territory border down to the Southern Ocean, with Perth on its
south-west corner.

13
00:02:06,099 --> 00:02:16,803
It is a third of the land, the largest subdivision of any country on earth
after Russia’s Sakha, and its capital Perth is the most isolated major city in
the world.

14
00:02:17,462 --> 00:02:25,055
Remember the empty west, a third of the country, with the loneliest capital on
earth down in its south-west corner.

15
00:02:25,744 --> 00:02:29,575
Let's bring South Australia into view.

16
00:02:32,062 --> 00:02:44,775
South Australia is the central state, running from the Northern Territory
border down to the Southern Ocean and reaching west to the coast and east to
the Victorian border, with Adelaide on the shore.

17
00:02:45,425 --> 00:02:59,624
It is the only state founded entirely by free settlers, with no convicts, and
it is also the driest state on the driest inhabited continent, yet the Barossa
Valley in it grows Australia’s best known wine.

18
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:08,388
Remember the settler state in the middle of the continent, the driest of them
all, with the Barossa vineyards in its south-east corner.

19
00:03:09,059 --> 00:03:11,311
Let's bring New South Wales into view.

20
00:03:15,973 --> 00:03:29,104
New South Wales runs down the eastern seaboard from the Queensland border to
the Victorian border, with Sydney on the coast and the Australian Capital
Territory enclosed inside it.

21
00:03:29,755 --> 00:03:41,435
Captain Cook named it in 1770 when he thought the coast looked like south
Wales, and it was the first British colony in Australia in 1788, so every
other eastern state was carved out of it.

22
00:03:42,084 --> 00:03:48,562
Remember the first colony and the coast that looks like Wales, with Sydney
Harbour in the middle of it.

23
00:03:49,243 --> 00:03:52,912
Let's bring Australian Capital Territory into view.

24
00:03:55,689 --> 00:04:07,798
The Australian Capital Territory is a territory, not a state, and the smallest
of the eight, lying entirely inland inside New South Wales with Canberra in
the middle of it.

25
00:04:08,458 --> 00:04:21,922
The land was taken out of New South Wales in 1911 to make room for a capital,
because Sydney and Melbourne could not agree where it should go, and the city
was designed by an American, Walter Burley Griffin.

26
00:04:22,577 --> 00:04:32,004
Remember the smallest of the eight, an inland patch of capital land cut out of
New South Wales to settle a quarrel between two rival cities.

27
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:34,814
Let's bring Victoria into view.

28
00:04:39,134 --> 00:04:50,349
Victoria is the small south-eastern state between South Australia and New
South Wales, facing Bass Strait and the Southern Ocean, with Melbourne near
its south-east corner.

29
00:04:51,008 --> 00:05:11,924
The gold rush of 1851 made Melbourne briefly the richest city in the world,
and Victoria is the smallest state on the mainland and the most densely
populated. The Twelve Apostles on its coast are limestone stacks the Southern
Ocean is still knocking down, and only eight of them are still standing.

30
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:23,029
Remember the smallest mainland state, crowded with people, with the gold rush
town of Melbourne and the sea stacks the waves are eating.

31
00:05:23,703 --> 00:05:26,466
Let's bring Tasmania into view.

32
00:05:30,601 --> 00:05:42,548
Tasmania is an island state, a whole island south of the mainland across Bass
Strait, with Hobart on its north-east shore and no land border with any other
region.

33
00:05:43,199 --> 00:05:59,003
The sea rose and cut it off from the mainland about 12,000 years ago, which is
why the Tasmanian devil survives here and nowhere else, and the cleanest air
in the world was measured at Cape Grim in its north-west.

34
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:07,845
Remember the island down south with the devil on it, cut off by the rising sea
long before any map was drawn.

35
00:06:13,429 --> 00:06:30,449
8 regions of Australia, one for each target of the map: Northern Territory,
Queensland, Western Australia, South Australia, New South Wales, Australian
Capital Territory, Victoria and Tasmania.

36
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:41,176
Remember the shape of Australia from the inside: the regions nest around each
other, and every name on the map belongs somewhere in this one country.
